<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yax Ehb Xook</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yax Ehb Xook was the founder of the royal dynasty of Tikal, the Maya city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guatemala">Guatemala</a>, as recorded by its later kings, who counted their place in the succession from him. He is thought to have lived in the 1st century CE, traditionally around 90, and one of the early royal tombs in the North Acropolis may be his. Little else is known of him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yax-ehb-xook.jpg" alt="Yax Ehb Xook" width="320" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mały koleżka · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yax_Ehb_Xook.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
